    "date": "1965",
    "description": "<div>A bilingual Hebrew-English maḥzor (festival prayerbook) for the first day of Rosh ha-Shanah according to the liturgical custom of Ashkenaz, as arranged by Wolf Heidenheim (1757-1832) and translated by Jenny Marmorstein (1920-2020). It is the first volume in this set of maḥzorim.</div><div><br /></div><div>This work is cross-posted to the Open Siddur where sections of it are the subject of a collaborative transcription initiative.</div><div><br /></div><div>This digital edition was prepared by Aharon Varady from page images made of an item held in the collection of the HUC-JIR Klau library, Cincinnati. (Thank you!)</div>",
